; Run-Probe - Doom 3 port, phase 2: what the port needs from GCC 16.2,
; libnix and SDL2 (PLAN.md section 8). Watch the screen: a small window shows
; red, green and blue for a second each, then a quiet tone plays for a second.
;   CD to this directory, then:   Execute Run-Probe
;   With a large file to time:     Execute Run-Probe FILE=<path of a pk4>
; Output goes to results/probe.txt.
.key FILE/K
.def FILE ""
.bra {
.ket }

FailAt 21
If NOT EXISTS cxx_probe
  Echo "Please CD into the cxx-probe directory first, then run:  Execute Run-Probe"
  Quit 20
EndIf
MakeDir results >NIL:
Avail FLUSH >NIL:
Avail >results/avail-before.txt
List LIBS:ogles2#? LIBS:v3dglslc >results/libs.txt
Echo "cxx_probe: C++, stack, memory, files, then a GL window (red, green, blue) and a tone"
If "{FILE}" EQ ""
  cxx_probe >results/probe.txt
Else
  cxx_probe --file "{FILE}" >results/probe.txt
EndIf
Echo "exit code $RC" >>results/probe.txt
Type results/probe.txt
Avail FLUSH >NIL:
Avail >results/avail-after.txt
